1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,681
For some weird reason america uses the imperial system.
他说，不知道为什么，美国用的是英制计量。

2
00:00:03,681 --> 00:00:08,240
Which means measuring distance in miles weight in pounds and volume in gallons.
也就是距离用英里，重量用磅，容量用加仑。

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,681
It's so funny to me cuz most of the world has no idea what any of this is.
他觉得好笑，因为世界上大部分人都不知道这些单位究竟是什么。

4
00:00:11,681 --> 00:00:15,520
Here in Europe and almost everywhere else in the world they use the metric system.
在欧洲，以及世界上几乎所有其他地方，人们用的是公制。

5
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:20,721
That means covering distances in kilometers weight in kilog and volume in liters.
这意味着距离按公里算，重量按千克算，容量按升算。〔kilog 原字幕截断，待复核〕

6
00:00:20,721 --> 00:00:24,640
All of these things can be pretty confusing for americans traveling in Europe and vice versa.
这些都可能让去欧洲旅行的美国人很困惑，反过来也一样。

7
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:29,441
But if you want to be a more worldly citizen I'm talking to you americans you should try to learn the metric system.
但如果想成为更熟悉世界的人——他说的是美国人——就应该试着学公制。

8
00:00:29,441 --> 00:00:32,880
It's really helpful for travel and it's also very simple and convenient.
公制对旅行很有帮助，也简单、方便。

9
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:36,561
Based on units of 10 making calculations and conversions much easier.
它基于十进制单位，让计算和换算容易得多。

10
00:00:36,561 --> 00:00:39,750
Also don't forget that in the us we use fahrenheit to tell weather.
还有，别忘了，美国用华氏温度来讲天气。

11
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,081
It's 22 I can't feel my hands or my face right now.
现在二十二度，我感觉不到自己的手和脸了。〔原片温度镜头例子，非当下天气〕

12
00:00:44,081 --> 00:00:46,321
It's about 85 f.
大约八十五华氏度。〔切换镜头的口述例子，非对上一数字的换算〕

13
00:00:46,321 --> 00:00:52,961
But in Europe and the rest of the entire world they use celsius or right now it's probably around 30.
但欧洲和世界其余地方用摄氏温度，比如现在大概三十度。

14
00:00:52,961 --> 00:00:55,441
Luckily I know both because I've been traveling the world for 12 years.
幸运的是，他两种都懂，因为自己已经环球旅行十二年。

15
00:00:55,441 --> 00:00:58,880
So it's easier for me to have conversations with non americans about things like weather.
因此，和非美国人聊天气之类的事情，对他更容易。

16
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,951
But this is always something that confuses me about the us.
但这仍然是美国让他一直困惑的一件事。

17
00:01:00,961 --> 00:01:07,431
And I think it's just because we like to be bigger and greater and different than everyone else in the world.
他觉得，这可能只是因为美国人喜欢比别人更大、更厉害、更与众不同。

18
00:01:07,441 --> 00:01:13,191
In the us coffee is consumed on the go with people grabbing their morning cups from drive thru places.
在美国，咖啡往往是匆忙中喝的，人们从汽车取餐窗口买早晨那一杯。

19
00:01:13,201 --> 00:01:18,151
Any kind of hot coffee americano I'll have a I'll have a latte.
热咖啡都行，美式……我来一杯，我要一杯拿铁。

20
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:21,921
They're just quickly running into starbucks ordering on the app and running out.
他们快步进星巴克，在应用里下单，然后又匆忙离开。

21
00:01:21,921 --> 00:01:25,510
We also pretty much only consume coffee in disposable paper cups.
他还说，我们几乎只用一次性纸杯喝咖啡。

22
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:28,791
In Europe it's a whole different story.
而在欧洲，情形就完全不同了。

23
00:01:28,801 --> 00:01:35,591
So you always drink while standing at the bar cheaper that way.
所以你总是站在吧台喝，这样更便宜。

24
00:01:35,601 --> 00:01:38,640
It's that bitter taste just like goes through your veins.
那股苦味简直像流进你的血管里。

25
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,870
It's like one sip wakes you up I'm serious.
就像一口便让你清醒，我是认真的。

26
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:43,441
This is like a perfect cappuccino with a foam top.
这简直是一杯完美的卡布奇诺，顶上有奶泡。

27
00:01:43,441 --> 00:01:46,481
Look at this first bite of a cappuccino has to be with a spoon.
看这个，卡布奇诺的第一口，得用勺子来吃。

28
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:48,711
The coffee culture is alive and real here.
这里的咖啡文化是真实而鲜活的。

29
00:01:48,721 --> 00:01:52,721
But people take their time when they drink and they see it as more of like a social thing.
但人们会慢慢喝，把它更多地视为一种社交活动。

30
00:01:52,721 --> 00:01:56,801
Even if they're by themselves they'll still go to the street corner sit down at a cafe outside.
即便一个人，他们仍会走到街角，在室外的咖啡馆坐下来。

31
00:01:56,801 --> 00:02:01,360
Of course enjoying the beautiful day and get a coffee and they'll just sit there and either read or work.
当然，享受好天气，买杯咖啡，然后坐在那里读书或者工作。

32
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,841
It's more of like an enjoyable leisure activity.
它更像是一种愉快的休闲活动。

33
00:02:03,841 --> 00:02:07,601
They always have like coffee mugs of course europeans don't like waste with plastic and paper.
他们总是用咖啡杯，作者说，欧洲人不喜欢浪费塑料和纸。

34
00:02:07,601 --> 00:02:10,640
They always just have everything feel more proper and more solidified.
他们总是让一切感觉更讲究、更有一种确定的质感。〔solidified 搭配不自然，待原声复核〕

35
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:15,321
And it's all about the experience of course got the coffee bringing it now to grandma.
一切都重在体验。好了，拿到咖啡，现在给奶奶送去。

36
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:21,350
When it comes to breakfast in the us everything is really heavy and greasy.
说到美国早餐，他觉得所有东西都很厚重、油腻。

37
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:26,081
Think about omelettes think about breakfast burritos pancakes hash browns bacon egg and cheese sandwiches.
想想煎蛋卷、早餐卷饼、松饼、薯饼、培根鸡蛋芝士三明治。

38
00:02:26,081 --> 00:02:31,031
These are heavy heavy heavy items that make you really full and have a lot of calories.
这些都是很厚重、厚重、厚重的食物，让人很饱，热量也高。

39
00:02:31,041 --> 00:02:36,630
M all the flavors of cheese and beans and eggs and sauce on one plate.
嗯，芝士、豆子、鸡蛋和酱汁的味道，全都在一个盘子里。

40
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:43,510
In Europe breakfast is nothing more than a little pastry buttery flaky puffy pastry or a little cookie or something sweet.
他说，欧洲的早餐不过是一小块酥点，黄油香、层层酥脆蓬松，或者小饼干等甜食。

41
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:47,161
This is everything I want right now a small espresso and a chocolate croissant.
这就是他现在最想要的：一小杯浓缩咖啡和一个巧克力可颂。

42
00:02:47,441 --> 00:02:49,681
That's so great it's so so so different.
太棒了，真的是太不一样了。

43
00:02:49,681 --> 00:02:55,520
And it's funny like here in Europe all the breakfast places that you'll go to like good breakfast places are like american branded.
有趣的是，他在欧洲会去的那些不错的早餐店，往往打着美式招牌。

44
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:58,880
It'll be like american breakfast american sausage american scrambled eggs.
比如美式早餐、美式香肠、美式炒蛋。

45
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:03,201
The breakfast is one of the biggest differences that I find between Europe and the us it's crazy different.
早餐是他发现的欧美最大差异之一，差别实在太大了。

46
00:03:03,201 --> 00:03:10,711
In Europe if it's not a croissant it's just like a piece of fruit or a little bit of cheese or one slice of bread.
他说，在欧洲，不是可颂的话，就可能是一块水果、少量芝士或一片面包。

47
00:03:10,721 --> 00:03:15,471
Soft and mushy absolutely worth it.
柔软，软乎乎的，完全值得。

48
00:03:17,201 --> 00:03:20,230
I will say though that the bakeries in Europe are awesome they're amazing.
不过他得说，欧洲的烘焙店真的很棒，太棒了。

49
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:26,151
They actually bake bread fresh every day in most countries around Europe.
他称欧洲大多数国家的面包店，每天都真正烤制新鲜面包。

50
00:03:26,161 --> 00:03:29,360
So it smells good on the streets and you know that you're getting quality bread.
因此街上闻起来很香，你也知道自己买到的是优质面包。

51
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:32,480
It's not like processed it's not like ordered on a big truck and shipped over.
不是那种加工好的，也不是从大货车批量订购、再运来的。

52
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:41,271
So I definitely side with Europe on this one although I got to admit I do love starbucks.
所以这方面他肯定站欧洲，不过也得承认，自己确实很爱星巴克。
